INT. RADIO STATION — NIGHT

The ON AIR light hums above an empty hallway. Rain needles the windows at the far end.

MARA, still in her coat, holds a cassette against the glass of the studio door.

MARA
You said you'd be here before the last song.

A voice answers through the headphones, soft beneath the static.

ELI (V.O.)
I am here. Just not where you expected.

Mara looks toward the blinking light on the console. She presses play.

MARA
(into the microphone)
Then let's start again.

EXT. CITY STREET — NIGHT

A single window glows above the sleeping storefronts.

CUT TO:
